WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.637
Night-operation requirements vary by jurisdiction, aircraft, purpose, location,

00:00:03.637 --> 00:00:04.963
and operating framework.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:08.058
Check current official aviation sources before flight.

00:00:08.058 --> 00:00:12.480
Do not rely on an old checklist, a social post,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.017
or software geofencing as a complete legal determination.

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:19.996
Requirements may address pilot qualification, aircraft registration or identification,

00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:24.417
anti-collision lighting, visual line of sight, airspace authorization, observers, records,

00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:27.070
and operations near people or vehicles.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.049
Local rules and property access may add separate obligations.

00:00:31.049 --> 00:00:36.354
Define the mission purpose, area, route, altitude strategy, required imagery, crew roles,

00:00:36.354 --> 00:00:37.239
and duration.

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:42.544
Confirm the site is authorized and that collection will not extend into

00:00:42.544 --> 00:00:45.197
unnecessary private areas or sensitive locations.

00:00:45.197 --> 00:00:49.176
Review airspace, temporary restrictions, airports, emergency activity, obstacles, terrain,

00:00:49.176 --> 00:00:51.829
weather, temperature, lighting, and nearby operations.

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:58.018
Visit or review the site in daylight when appropriate so hidden wires, branches, structures,

00:00:58.018 --> 00:01:01.113
and landing hazards are known before darkness.

00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:04.208
Set go or no-go and abort criteria.

00:01:04.208 --> 00:01:09.072
These may include minimum visibility, acceptable wind, battery condition, lighting function,

00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:13.935
navigation confidence, signal quality, crew readiness, and a clear recovery area.

00:01:13.935 --> 00:01:17.914
Use limits appropriate to official requirements and manufacturer guidance.

00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:23.220
Document the sources checked, approvals, aircraft, crew, weather, site findings, risk controls,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.872
return settings, emergency options, and decision.

00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:31.620
When authority or conditions are unclear, delay the flight and obtain qualified guidance.
